      "text": "To solve this problem, we will use the concept of inverse proportionality.\n\nAn inversely proportional relationship can be represented by the equation:\n$$\\alpha = k / \\beta$$\nwhere $k$ is the constant of proportionality and $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are the variables.\n\nWe are given that $\\alpha = 4$ when $\\beta = 9$. We can use this information to find the value of $k$:\n$$4 = k / 9$$\nTo solve for $k$, we can multiply both sides of the equation by $9$:\n$$36 = k$$\nNow we know that the constant of proportionality is $k = 36$.\n\nTo find $\\alpha$ when $\\beta = -72$, we can substitute these values into the equation:\n$$\\alpha = 36 / -72$$\n$$\\alpha = -1/2$$\n\nSo, when $\\beta = -72$, the value of $\\alpha$ is $\\boxed{-1/2}$.",
